# OWNER REVIEW
# The Neighbourhood Watch's captain, by his hut, with the logbook (Key 7; levels/primrose/keys/logbook.gd). In the
# suit, Nim passes for head office: each "slip" flag costs Composure, and two slips or naming the Claw and he blows
# his whistle. The logbook records every visit to every party, and eleven visits to the Watch hut by his wife.

~ start
[if primrose/logbook] => after
[if not primrose/in_suit] => garb
Captain: Evening. Neighbourhood Watch. Nobody comes into the Close without it going in the book.
Captain: And who might you be?
- Head office. The Coalition sent me for the book. => one
- Oh, I'm, um, a friend? Of the street? => one_soft

~ one_soft
set primrose/log_slip1
=> one

~ one
Captain: Head office? Nobody told me about head office.
- Nobody tells you anything, Captain. That's what I'm here to fix. => two
- Sorry! Shall I come back with a letter? => two_soft
- The Velvet Claw sent me. => refused

~ two_soft
[if primrose/log_slip1] => refused
set primrose/log_slip2
=> two

~ two
Captain: Well. If it's for the cause.
[narrator] The logbook: every visit to every party on the Close, in a careful hand. Dates, times, and who went home with a carrier bag.
[narrator] And every Tuesday for eleven weeks: "Visit to the Watch hut by Mrs Pettigrew. Brought sandwiches. Stayed one hour."
Captain: My wife. She brings me sandwiches. It's the Watch. She's watching me. It's allowed.
set primrose/logbook

~ refused
Captain [cold]: Head office, my whiskers.
[narrator] He blows his whistle, long and loud. Up and down the Close, porch lights come on.
set primrose/log_refused
=> END

~ garb
Captain: Off the lawn, please. This is a Watch lawn.

~ after
Captain: I've started a new book. It's going to be a quieter book.
